course: dictionary
lesson: 8952
title: Word clues in a nature text
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a creature, and the text tells you what it is like. «The silverback is the grown-up male leader of a gorilla group; the silver hair on his back appears at about 12 years old.» The clues are grown-up, male, leader and silver hair on the back. Put them together and a silverback is a grown-up male gorilla who leads his family.
explain: Look at the word parts too. Silver and back make silverback, which hints at the colour and where it is. Check it with the sentences: «A silverback gorilla beats his chest with cupped hands» shows the word means a gorilla, not a silver coat or a spoon. A word part can give a clue, but the sentence has the final say.
explain: Some words are used as jokes. «Sometimes people jokingly call a strong older man who leads a group a silverback.» The word jokingly is the clue. It tells you the person is not really a gorilla; he is being compared to a gorilla leader because he is strong and in charge.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A silverback is a grown-up male gorilla and the leader of a gorilla family.
fact: The silver-grey hair on a silverback's back is what gives him his name.
fact: A silverback beats his chest with cupped hands, and the popping sound tells rivals how big he is, often so a real fight is not needed.
fact: Informally, people sometimes call a strong older man who leads a group a silverback, as a joke.
exercise: The silverback is the grown-up male leader of a gorilla group. Which gorilla is a silverback? | A baby gorilla who is still small | A young male who has not grown up yet | A female gorilla with a baby | *A grown-up male who leads the group
exercise: «A silverback gorilla beats his chest with cupped hands, and the popping drum sound tells rivals how big he is.» What does the chest beat tell rivals? | That he wants to play a game | That he is hungry | That it is time to sleep | *That he is big and strong
exercise: «A silverback gorilla beating his chest looks terrifying, but he is mostly a gentle vegetarian.» Why is the chest beat often used instead of a real fight? | Because gorillas cannot make any sound | Because gorillas love music | *Because a show of strength can avoid a real fight | Because he is very hungry
test: Which word means a strong older man who leads a group, used as a joke? | Chimp | Lion | *Silverback | Gorilla
test: «A silverback is an adult male gorilla whose back turns silver from about 12 years old.» At about what age does a silverback's back turn silver? | About 1 year old | *About 12 years old | About 18 years old | About 100 years old
exam: In the sentence «The silverback is the grown-up male leader of a gorilla group», what does silverback mean? | A kind of ancient castle | A small baby monkey | A silver-coloured car | *A grown-up male gorilla who leads the group
